solution_steps:
We can use polynomial long division to divide $6x^4 - 14x^3 - 4x^2 + 2x - 26$ by $2x - 6$.
$$\begin{array}{c|ccccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{3x^3} & -x^2 & - x + 1 \\\cline{2-6}
2x - 6 & 6x^4 & - 14x^3 & - 4x^2 & 2x & - 26 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{6x^4} & - 18x^3 \\ \cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & 4x^3 & - 4x^2 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 4x^3 & - 12x^2 \\ \cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & 8x^2 & 2x \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 8x^2 & -24x \\ \cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 0 & 26x & - 26 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 26x & - 78 \\ \cline{5-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 0 & 52
\end{array}$$
So, when we divide $6x^4 - 14x^3 - 4x^2 + 2x - 26$ by $2x - 6$, the remainder is $\boxed{52}$.
The answer is: 52

