We can start by finding the values of $f(10)$ and $g(10)$ using the given functions.
\begin{align*}
f(10) &= 3(10)^2 - 2(10) + 4 = 300 - 20 + 4 = 284, \\
g(10) &= (10)^2 - k(10) - 6 = 100 - 10k - 6 = 94 - 10k.
\end{align*}
Now we can substitute these values into the equation $f(10) - g(10) = 10$ and solve for $k$.
\begin{align*}
f(10) - g(10) &= 284 - (94 - 10k) = 284 - 94 + 10k = 10, \\
10k &= 10 - 190 = -180, \\
k &= \frac{-180}{10} = \boxed{-18}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: -18

