solution_steps:
We know that $\tan 45^\circ = 1,$ so $\tan (45^\circ + 30^\circ) = \frac{1 + \tan 30^\circ}{1 - \tan 30^\circ}.$
Since $\tan 30^\circ = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}},$ we have \[\tan 75^\circ = \frac{1 + \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}{1 - \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}} = \frac{\sqrt{3} + 1}{\sqrt{3} - 1} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3} + 1}{\sqrt{3} + 1} = \frac{4 + 2 \sqrt{3}}{2} = \boxed{2 + \sqrt{3}}.\]
The answer is: 2+\sqrt{3}

We can use long division to divide $7x^3 + 3x^2 - 5x - 8$ by $x + 2$:

\[
\begin{array}{c|cc cc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{7x^2} & -11x & +17 \\
\cline{2-5}
x + 2 & 7x^3 & +3x^2 & -5x & -8 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{-7x^3} & -14x^2 & & \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & -11x^2 & -5x & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & +11x^2 & +22x & \\
\cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & +17x & -8 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & -17x & -34 \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 0 & +26 \\
\end{array}
\]

So, the quotient is $7x^2 - 11x + 17$ and the remainder is $26$.
The answer is: 7x^2-11x+17

